{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he turned and went out from Pharaoh's presence.</b> As soon as he warned him of the great plague, he went out from before him. And this was a way of wisdom and stratagem on Moses' part, so that they would take counsel to send them forth — for in the plague of hail preceding this one, they reckoned themselves as good as dead, all the more so in this plague coming after it, to wipe out all that the hail had left. And so they did: they took counsel that he should send them off. Therefore the king commanded that they return — that is what is written: ״ויושב את משה ואת אהרן״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:24.341283686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}